SUMMARY:Native Seed Propagation
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to propagate native plants from seed and gain practical skills for growing them from seed collection through germination. Topics include seed collection methods\, post-collection handling\, cleaning equipment and techniques\, seed storage\, seed sowing techniques\, sowing media\, cultural requirements of seedlings\, and dormancy requirements. The workshop includes both classroom instruction and outdoor learning in the display gardens. \nOpen to participants of all experience levels. \nThis course counts as an elective for the Certificate in Native Plants program. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/native-seed-propagation/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
CATEGORIES:Learn
